From: ms178-agent <agent@local>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 15:45:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Cross-backend ABI round: CASP, MOVW, .org, branch binding
 triage, va_arg struct{long double} alignment

AArch64 assembler:
- add CASP/CASPA/CASPAL/CASPL (LSE compare-and-swap pair) encoding per
  LLVM AArch64InstrFormats.td (0|SZ size field, NP=0); Capstone
  round-trip verified for every ordering x width; pair operands are
  validated architecturally (even start, consecutive, uniform width,
  no SP/xzr members) because Xs+1/Xt+1 have no encoding fields
- extend the register-propagation skip to the whole cas/casp family:
  CASP's compare-pair members are in-out and the second sits after the
  first comma, exactly where the source rewriter operates
- implement .org new-lc[,fill] with GAS semantics: token-boundary-aware
  location-counter/label substitution, immediate evaluation, backward
  move and forward-reference errors; vector-table shape verified
- branches to global/weak symbols now keep CALL26/JUMP26 relocations
  even when defined in the same section (GAS preemption parity); the
  binding check happens at resolution time since .globl may follow use
- movz/movk :abs_g*: modifiers resolve at write time: local aliases and
  labels encode inline with overflow checks (non-_nc), globals and
  externals become MOVW relocations; movn rejects modifiers (MOVW
  semantics cannot express its inverted immediate); suffix parsing is
  an exact grammar, so mistyped mnemonics error instead of silently
  encoding as relaxed CAS

AArch64 linker:
- repair MOVW relocation type numbers to IHI0056B (G1_NC was resolved
  with G1's shift, G3 with G2's) and add the missing G1/G2/SABS_G0-2
  handlers; dead-wrong constants that could never fire before the
  assembler gained MOVW emission

Shared ABI (call_abi.rs):
- compute_stack_arg_space is padding-aware; the old unpadded round can
  under-allocate when over-aligned structs interleave with scalars
- named stack parameters whose alignment exceeds XLEN are aligned to
  min(align, 2*XLEN) in the shared callee loop; named_params_stack_bytes
  derives from the ParamClass offsets so it cannot drift from layout

RISC-V / ARM callers:
- honor the previously-ignored struct_arg_aligns with per-arg padding
  from the shared compute_stack_arg_padding; struct { long double }
  variadic args now land 16-byte aligned where va_arg reads them
  (fix_riscv_va_arg_long_double_struct, test_misalign_r10 shape,
  verified in generated assembly)

i686:
- drop duplicated #[test] attribute (zero-warning contract for the test
  profile)

Tests: 12 new unit tests (CASP words, CAS drift pins, .org, branch
triage, MOVW tramp_alias/external/overflow), regression tests
i686_double_param_high_word (locks f01(10.0)==10 with both stores) and
ld_struct_va_arg_align (locks caller/callee alignment agreement).
Unit 1262/0/6; regression 476/0/0 AB-diff. Queue: 8 of 9 tasks closed
(fix_dash deferred: needs a RISC-V execution environment).
